NeurIPS 2026 Paper (typage/neurips) - license

This template contains files from two sources.

  main.tex, refs.bib, manifest.json, typage.json, LICENSE
      Written by 7D24H. CC0-1.0: dedicated to the public domain; papers
      written from this template need no attribution.
      https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

  neurips_2026.sty, checklist.tex
      The official NeurIPS 2026 style file (2026-01-29) and paper checklist,
      published by the Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems
      for authors preparing submissions, in
      https://media.neurips.cc/Conferences/NeurIPS2026/Formatting_Instructions_For_NeurIPS_2026.zip
      The files carry no license statement; all rights remain with NeurIPS.
      They are redistributed unmodified, as published, so that the template
      compiles offline. Always check the current Call for Papers at
      https://neurips.cc for the rules that apply to your submission.

The packages the sample loads (natbib, hyperref, ...) come from the
built-in Tectonic bundle under their own licenses.
